{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook","id":1287830,"title":"How likely is a 2-volume corebook?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-13T20:37:47-08:00","id":1287830,"title":"How likely is a 2-volume corebook?","content":"One thing that has come up in several of the reviews I've read/watched is that the Ex3 corebook is so massive (and/or the PoD quality so low) that the book can't even hold itself together even when handled very gently. So, given that little issue, is there any possibility that it might someday be offered as a 2-volume bundle?<br /> I don't own it yet and I would like to get it, but the worry that I might end up with a book that is doomed to fall apart is one issue that has made me hesitate to get it so far (please don't bother mentioning PDFs, I don't read PDFs so it's physical or nothing for me). It just seems like a book that can't hold itself together under its own weight is a pretty significant design flaw. Also, I figure OPP will not be making such massive books in the future given that we now know that PoD cant handle that size, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1964-the-voice","name":"The Voice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T21:47:09-08:00","id":1287844,"title":"","content":"There's always-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> please don't bother mentioning PDFs </div> </div> </div>Oh PICKY PICKY PICKY! :P<br /> <br /> Seriously though, at this point it seems... Unlikely? The devs right now seem to be more focused on progressing forward with new content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T22:15:51-08:00","id":1287854,"title":"","content":"At least my deluxe hardcover corebook looks cool on my shelf and can be used to bludgeon intruders to death in an emergency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T22:34:58-08:00","id":1287858,"title":"","content":"My copy's held up okay, but it's the Deluxe, so I don't know how that compares to the baseline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T23:29:31-08:00","id":1287872,"title":"","content":"I'd less want a 2-volume core book, and more a slimmed down core rules for when I'm not using Solars and I don't need all the setting material in the main core book.<br /> <br /> I have the 2-volume copy of V20, and I don't end up using it because finding rules in big tomes is hard enough, having two books to flip through does not help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T02:39:24-08:00","id":1287894,"title":"","content":"I have the lower quality POD print and I'm surprised that it's still intact after years of fairly regular use on the table. In fact, it's survived even better than many of my sewn-bound RPG books.<br /> I don't mean to belittle those, who have had their books break. Just saying that miracles can and do happen and sometimes you get lucky.<br /> <br /> It's the Solar book after all, Solar's are supposed to achieve the impossible!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","name":"Taleksi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T02:56:42-08:00","id":1287896,"title":"","content":"I would LOVE a two-volume book, perhaps the core rules in one and Solar Charms/rules in the other (I imagine they would be about the same size).<br /> <br /> I have the deluxe book and even that is beginning to show signs of splitting at the middle, and has always been too unwieldy to sit and read with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T03:17:11-08:00","id":1287901,"title":"","content":"Oh wow. I've gotta start being more careful with mine. I've been able to stick it in my bag and ride my bike across town with it, but maybe I shouldn't push my luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T04:17:28-08:00","id":1287904,"title":"","content":"I think they should do the same as they did with Trinity and Scion.<br /> <br /> A Core book with all the basic rules, basically for playing mortals; and a Solars book, similar to What Fire Has Wrought and Fangs at the Gate.<br /> It just makes more sense to me. I ran an entire campaign with just mortals, so I would have appreciated such a division.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T04:38:14-08:00","id":1287905,"title":"","content":"I've been hoping for this since the book was released. I think there are parts of the core I haven't even read yet because the book is so ungainly, and I hate taking it off the shelf (I have both the deluxe and the PoD).<br /> <br /> Someone once suggested to me that you could cut the pages out and have them rebound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T06:43:16-08:00","id":1287920,"title":"","content":"I would like to echo that while I own the deluxe third edition core book, it is useful as shelf decoration only. It is a very heavy book, so I use the .pdf instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T06:59:23-08:00","id":1287925,"title":"","content":"I can attest to the lack of structure for the regular core book. I think it took all of a day for the spine to separate from the cover on one side. Certainly less time than character creation took. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd like to see a two-volume copy with Solar character creation, traits and charms in one volume with all the rest in another. So stuff in the traits section would be best in both (merits and similar). I feel that this would cut it into manageable chunks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T07:05:57-08:00","id":1287927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1287905#post1287905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone once suggested to me that you could cut the pages out and have them rebound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately there is rules text in boxes in the charm text (why it wasn\u2019t in the rules areas I have no idea).<br /> <br /> I also think that just the rules without solar stuff and setting info would be fantastic. Especially if they could rewrite/clarify some areas. However that would also delay other new books and that would suck since we are just now getting books in the pipeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T09:15:24-08:00","id":1287967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1287904#post1287904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they should do the same as they did with Trinity and Scion.<br /> <br /> A Core book with all the basic rules, basically for playing mortals; and a Solars book, similar to What Fire Has Wrought and Fangs at the Gate.<br /> It just makes more sense to me. I ran an entire campaign with just mortals, so I would have appreciated such a division.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think that Scion didn't need to be two volumes, personally. There's a lot of weirdness to its structure and such as a result of it as well I think. Exalted as a game is also kind of billed on playing well, Solars default and upfront, while Scion and trinity present the &quot;default&quot; games more as games in of themselvs. The split would be odd too since some things unviersal to all Exalted beyond the core (spells, Martial Arts, Evocations) would probably still need to be in the Solar book if youw ant to keep things thinned down, not really making it optional.<br /> <br /> What Exalted 3e needed more was the companion-style book that they did for Kickstarters from Scion 2e onward. A <i>lot</i> of why the book is so big was the adding a dozen animals, nearly a dozens spirits, eight Martial Arts styles, piles of spells, and so on.<br /> <br /> As for folks who wanted a simplififed set of the rules, the Jumpstart, <b>Tomb of Dreams</b>, actually more or less has all the important base mechancis in it save Merits, Limit Break and specific weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T09:17:09-08:00","id":1287971,"title":"","content":"My standard printing ripped out of its binding quite quickly so I've also considered having someone rebind it into two separate volumes. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1287927#post1287927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately there is rules text in boxes in the charm text (why it wasn\u2019t in the rules areas I have no idea).</div> </div> </div> </div> You needn't split the pages precisely in the middle. Just choose a chapter break and put about half of the text in one volume and half in the other. I must be misunderstanding you here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1287927#post1287927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that just the rules without solar stuff and setting info would be fantastic. Especially if they could rewrite/clarify some areas. However that would also delay other new books and that would suck since we are just now getting books in the pipeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that Tomb of Dreams -the &quot;jumpstart&quot; kit- does exactly this. Is there some way in which it fails that I haven't picked up on?<br /> <br /> edit: Drat, Siderial'ed by Blaque","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 02-14-2019, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:25:07-08:00","id":1288033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1287927#post1287927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately there is rules text in boxes in the charm text (why it wasn\u2019t in the rules areas I have no idea).<br /> <br /> I also think that just the rules without solar stuff and setting info would be fantastic. Especially if they could rewrite/clarify some areas. However that would also delay other new books and that would suck since we are just now getting books in the pipeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>God I hate that this is true.<br /> <br /> Did <i>no one</i> in the editing phase realize that the Core book was supposed to be more than <i>just </i>Solars? Like, oh hey I'm gonna play a Dragon Blood and I want to train a familiar. I guess I better go hunt through the Solar Survival Charms to figure out how to do that? :-(","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:43:18-08:00","id":1288042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1288033#post1288033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God I hate that this is true.<br /> <br /> Did <i>no one</i> in the editing phase realize that the Core book was supposed to be more than <i>just </i>Solars? Like, oh hey I'm gonna play a Dragon Blood and I want to train a familiar. I guess I better go hunt through the Solar Survival Charms to figure out how to do that? :-(</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just a bit of weird editting, as the exact same rules are actually repeated in the bestiary and needed not be in the Solar Charms to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T13:12:10-08:00","id":1288048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1288042#post1288042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just a bit of weird editting, as the exact same rules are actually repeated in the bestiary and needed not be in the Solar Charms to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking this up makes it even worse, because we're both wrong.<br /> <br /> Both sections give rules for training latent abilities, it's true. However, they give <i>different difficulties</i> for these rolls.<br /> <br /> Beast Mastering Behavior pg 410:<br /> <br /> &quot;The trainer makes an extended roll with an interval of one month and a goal of 10, modified by the animal\u2019s attitude\u2014docile and tamed beasts presenting no penalties, familiars representing a number of bonus dice equal to the trainer\u2019s Intimacy to the animal, and hostile, wild, or otherwise untrainable animals representing a penalty of -2 or -3. &quot;<br /> <br /> Latent and Magical Abilities pg 554: <br /> <br /> &quot;The trainer makes an extended roll with an interval of one month and a goal of 10, with a difficulty determined by the animal\u2019s attitude\u2014docile and tamed beasts would be difficulty 1, a wild wolf would be difficulty 2, while a tyrant lizard would be difficulty 5. Training a familiars provides a number of bonus dice equal to the trainer\u2019s Intimacy to the animal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hell, the Survival charm isn't even written to fit an extended action. It should be talking about difficulty for the extended action, rather than penalties.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T14:41:48-08:00","id":1288085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1287927#post1287927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that just the rules without solar stuff and setting info would be fantastic. Especially if they could rewrite/clarify some areas. However that would also delay other new books and that would suck since we are just now getting books in the pipeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the thing. Splitting the core into two coherent books (Core Rules + Solar Exalted, like NWoD did) would actually be a pretty involved endeavor. You'd need new text written, all new layout, maybe even new art depending on how all the section breaks fall after the editing and rearranging is done. So while I agree it would be really nice, I don't see it happening within the next, say, 10 years.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I would settle for a totally janky (but totally attainable) PoD option that chunked the existing book into two or three arbitrary pieces (maybe chapters 1-5, 6, and 7+).<br /> <br /> Having content across two or three conveniently-sized books is way better than not being able to find anything in one gigantic book you can barely hold. At least, to my way of thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T15:21:20-08:00","id":1288097,"title":"","content":"Everytime this was mentioned for the previous edition, there was ALWAYS a guy who came in and said &quot;I wouldn't buy a book called Exalted that did not include how to play the Exalted \u00f1e\u00f1e\u00f1e&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm very glad this hasn't happened. I think this forum has evolved into its Raichu equivalent.<br /> <br /> Yes, I agree and think a re-formating of the core is very necessary. Bigger books are not better books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T15:49:04-08:00","id":1288108,"title":"","content":"I admit Revised 3E \u201cExalted Core\u201d and \u201cSolars: Return of Glory\u201d would be great provided they were 100% backwards compatible with all the existing hardbacks and supplements other than the original 3E Core.<br /> <br /> That said, this industry\u2019s moving increasingly digitial so not accepting that option with POD is going to make solutions difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-14-2019, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T21:30:14-08:00","id":1288164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1288097#post1288097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everytime this was mentioned for the previous edition, there was ALWAYS a guy who came in and said &quot;I wouldn't buy a book called Exalted that did not include how to play the Exalted \u00f1e\u00f1e\u00f1e&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm very glad this hasn't happened. I think this forum has evolved into its Raichu equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was tired of this topic, I've said my piece on it more than once, and I'm literally tired and about to go to bed, but you just activated my spite card.<br /> <br /> I am *absolutely* one of those people who firmly believes that a core book without the Exalted in it is the wrong way to go. I will die on this hill, come back as a Moonshadow, die on this hill again, and leave my hungry ghost to carry on after if that's what it takes. <br /> <br /> *That said*, I would absolutely be up for some way to isolate the core rules, especially in tidy and discrete chunks so you could just, say, easily pull up the combat rules, or the crafting rules, or <i>whatever </i> and know that that's all that's there in this file or booklet or whatever.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T21:37:06-08:00","id":1288165,"title":"","content":"What Mockery said. With emphasis on the spite card bit. Infantilizing the arguments of people who disagree with you is seldom a good way to approach forum debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T01:14:55-08:00","id":1288206,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't object to reformatting the book as &quot;setting + basic engine&quot; and &quot;charms and other Solar-specific stuff&quot; for simple ease of storage and use, so long as it was clear they were parts of a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T05:53:43-08:00","id":1288231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1288164#post1288164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am *absolutely* one of those people who firmly believes that a core book without the Exalted in it is the wrong way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you think a single case for both volumes would be a nice solution for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:27:06-08:00","id":1288290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1288231#post1288231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you think a single case for both volumes would be a nice solution for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the execution, I can understand the appeal. If it's a divide for pragmatic concerns of making sure the binding doesn't collapse, then cool. Otherwise...<br /> <br /> (Okay, we're about to hit the part where Mockery rants about why Solars need to be in the core. People can feel free to skip the remaining meandering paragraphs of an angry office muppet clacking away at a keyboard.)<br /> <br /> I continue to insist that the Solars need to be in the corebook. While they are the inheritors of the legacy from their predecessors in the First Age, that era's relevance in the present day Age of Sorrows is best served as scraps, rare and impossible treasures, and ancient records made fallible by the passage of time and personal agendas. Going into greater detail re: the First Age inevitably comes at the price of some relevance of the second: Metagalapa goes from a flying mountain with a culture of eagle riders to a bunch of distractions in the way of an aerial fortress. Icemind ceases to be a one-of-a-kind creation formed by a couple brilliant minds on an irreproducible bender, and is now the merest access terminal that they drunkenly hit the on switch for. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in the present day Solars explicitly don't have a unifying culture the way most of the other Exalted do, and that's by design. To be sure, other Exalted have their Outcastes, Ronin, and Casteless, but even then, their lack of membership is generally a large part of their character. Outcastes are perhaps the least beholden to this; you could theoretically do a core based around the Dragon-Blooded (original plan, blah blah, we know) and just flesh out the Realm itself later. But the splatbooks are there to tell you specifically about the playable options and factions these characters have that weren't in the core: the Lunars have the Pact, their shahan-ya and adherents; the Dragon-Blooded have the Realm, Lookshy, the Dreaming Sea, and the Forest Witches; the Sidereals have their Bronze and Gold Factions, and the life of a functionary of Heaven. Again, Solars do not have that.<br /> <br /> Further, IIRC the most commonly suggested setting material and fluff for a Solar splatbook would focus on the First Age and underscore their legacy as ancient sorcerous god-kings. Which, cool, but\u2014BUT\u2014the context in which a splat is presented creates expectations about how a default game is intended to go. While players and ST's could and certainly would have some stories focused squarely on what is rather than what is, a Solar splatbook that focuses on the glories of the First Age places the expected Solar narrative into the role of trying to restore them, and while I've already said as much up above, let me re-state this: focusing on the First Age is a bad move. Dreams of the First Age turned the main setting of the game from a tragic pulp fantasy seeking its glories until the curtain fell, to a messy, broken state* waiting for some Solars to show up with Craft Charms and waggle their fingers at stuff to make everyone look like chumps and put everything back the way it should be.**<br /> <br /> Solars do not have the background to merit an individual splatbook like the other kinds, this is by design, and it's a good thing. It gives room for the setting to be introduced with a more-or-less neutral eye. Deep setting knowledge and assumptions are completely unnecessary for the splat as a whole, and it's an easy point of entry. The Solars do not have, do not need, and should not have their own fatsplat book.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*Admittedly 2e had a lot of problems along these lines, starting just about from Wonders of the First Age, but Dreams made it all into a Frankensteinian whole.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">** It also sent Desus from a representative of Lawgivers driven monstrous by the Great Curse in his later years to being possibly the worst human being ever who didn't need the curse of the dying Primordials to be utterly contemptible. The tragedy is gone because there was never anything lost that was worth keeping.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:09:12-08:00","id":1288333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1288231#post1288231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you think a single case for both volumes would be a nice solution for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Also see my previous point about V20's two volumes and the utility thereof.<br /> <br /> Or for an added example, look at the CofD. In 1e they did a mortals only core book, which you then needed for any of the supernatural splats. Turning all of supernatural games into this. While it was nice for the collector types (including myself) to not have to repurchase the core rules every time, juggling multiple books isn't great either. In CofD 2e they went to putting the core rules in all the different core books again, making it much easier to run a game of Forsaken if that's all you're going to run because you can run it with one book.<br /> <br /> My groups got turned off of both Exalted 1.5 and 2.5 because it was too much work just to sort through the books, and playing non-Solars was sometimes a push because of having to have multiple large texts to look through to find things. While Exalted is too big of a game to avoid that second part, minimizing the number of books even if the average book is larger, is frequently a better choice for at-table utility.<br /> <br /> When you look at the very successful D&amp;D model of breaking the books into multiple books... it's players vs. the DM in terms of content. The PHB + DMG model wouldn't work if the PHB was 560 pages and the DMG was 80 (aka reflective of how Exalted tends to prioritize player facing information vs. ST focused information), or if all the Classes were in the DMG instead of the PHB. The PHB + DMG approach only really works is the PHB is complete enough that you don't need the DMG, but rather you want the DMG to make the game you could just play with the PHB even better.<br /> <br /> Exalted just isn't written that way. Is 3e a giant tome? Yes. But there's no effective way to do a two-volume setup that serves anyone by die hard fans and collectors, without inconveniencing newer and more casual fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T12:27:24-08:00","id":1288969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1288033#post1288033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God I hate that this is true.<br /> <br /> Did <i>no one</i> in the editing phase realize that the Core book was supposed to be more than <i>just </i>Solars? Like, oh hey I'm gonna play a Dragon Blood and I want to train a familiar. I guess I better go hunt through the Solar Survival Charms to figure out how to do that? :-(</div> </div> </div> </div>But... the core book <i>wasn't</i> supposed to be more than just Solars. The Exalted core book has always been a Solar book. Rules for playing other things come later. Has been that way since 1st edition.<br /> <br /> The core book lets you play Solars and kinda half-heartedly mortals. Each Exalt gets its own splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T14:05:35-08:00","id":1288993,"title":"","content":"Except... the core book is supposed to be more than just Solars. It's supposed to include the basic rules everyone uses... which is why you need it to play the other Exalted.<br /> <br /> I think the editing in this regard isn't as bad as armyofwhispers was originally saying (as noted the Solar Charm section was mostly just repeating a rule in the more general section). But there really shouldn't be any rules just in the Solar Charm section that apply to everyone. One or two isn't the end of the world, but it isn't a good thing, and it isn't justified by the core book being the Solar book as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T12:05:59-08:00","id":1289260,"title":"","content":"I just wish that the Charms were in their own volume with a nice slip cover for both books. That would make the rest of the core book easier to page through. I bet they thought through this and didn't go the route because of cost...it does take more money to bind a book twice than it does to do it once.<br /> <br /> In any case, I may eventually go ahead and make my own version of a 2-volume book. I have done something like this before when I made a complete 2.5 Solar charm book with errata and such. I can do it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--Lurker Extraordinaire!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/344-darkwolff","name":"DarkWolff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T12:45:11-08:00","id":1289270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkWolff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1287830-how-likely-is-a-2-volume-corebook?p=1289260#post1289260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wish that the Charms were in their own volume with a nice slip cover for both books. That would make the rest of the core book easier to page through. I bet they thought through this and didn't go the route because of cost...it does take more money to bind a book twice than it does to do it once.<br /> <br /> In any case, I may eventually go ahead and make my own version of a 2-volume book. I have done something like this before when I made a complete 2.5 Solar charm book with errata and such. I can do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I've actually already done that for my own games. Though Exalted's not the only game I've sat and made useful-for-my-table summary thingsl iekt hat for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}